" terminal Vim/Neovim-only autocmds {{{
" IdeaVim (checked 2.47.1) runs FocusGained/FocusLost/BufEnter autocmds too,
" but has no :checktime or :highlight - outside this block these threw E492
" into a hit-enter panel on every IntelliJ app switch (e.g. Cmd-. for
" Dropzone), which grabbed focus and swallowed the next keys (jk, <Space>s).

" reload buffers changed on disk by something else (another vim/nvim
" instance, a shell append, iCloud sync) instead of silently overwriting
" them on save with a stale in-memory copy. {{{
" `autoread` alone only takes effect at specific trigger points, not
" continuously - it doesn't retroactively cover a buffer that's just been
" sitting open. `checktime` forces that check on focus/idle so autoread
" actually gets exercised in practice, not just when you happen to run a
" command that triggers it. {{{
set autoread
augroup checktime_on_focus
  autocmd!
  autocmd FocusGained,BufEnter,CursorHold,CursorHoldI * if mode() != 'c' | checktime | endif
augroup END
" }}}
