" vim when NERDTree is the last window" autocmd below, quitting Vim entirely
" instead of just returning to the previous buffer.
" (previously used Ctrl-Q for :q, but IntelliJ's keymap binds ctrl+q globally to
" HideActiveWindow - see macOS - ian.xml - which swallows the keystroke before
" IdeaVim sees it, hiding the terminal tool window instead. Bare Q has no IDE-level
" conflict: IntelliJ's default keymap never binds an unmodified single letter in
" the editor context, since normal typing needs it.)
