" set shift size to 4 too;
" meaning the indent level will be 4 columns wide.
" so that's what you get when you do '>>' in normal mode.
" but there's no `\t` character when you do this. right?
set shiftwidth=4

" fix the lag on a bare <Esc> press in command-line/normal mode. Vim can't
" tell a raw <Esc> byte from the start of a longer terminal escape sequence
" (arrow keys, alt combos) until 'ttimeoutlen' elapses; it defaults to
" inheriting 'timeoutlen' (1000ms). This only affects that ambiguity check -
" 'timeoutlen' (still default) is what jk/kj->Esc waits on, so that mapping's
" already-fast feel is untouched.
set ttimeoutlen=10
