" Neovim's terminal UI (unlike plain Vim's here) renders truecolor
" faithfully, so let it use the guifg/guibg hex values below instead of
" being limited to the nearest 256-color cterm approximation - needed for
" shades (e.g. StatusLineNC's dim green) that have no close match in the
" 6x6x6 cterm color cube. Scoped to has('nvim') only, so plain terminal Vim
" keeps rendering from ctermbg as before.
if has('nvim')
  set termguicolors
endif

colorscheme industry
" transparency variable only works for MacVim
" if has("gui_running")
" 	set transparency=18
" endif

" hide terminal Vim's background, effectively making it transparent if you have the terminal background set as transparent.
" but enabling it reduces the contrast
hi Normal guibg=NONE ctermbg=NONE

" highlight status bar of active window
" must be placed after colorscheme setting, otherwise overriden
highlight StatusLine ctermfg=black guifg=#ffffff ctermbg=34 guibg=#1f8a4c
" StatusLineNC = status bar of this vim's OTHER (non-current) :split windows.
" 'industry' colorscheme's default (ctermbg=242 guibg=#6c6c6c) is a fairly
" light gray, close in weight to the bright green StatusLine above - barely
" reads as "inactive" next to it. Dim it further so the current split is
" unambiguously the one with focus. Give it a faint green tint (rather than
" plain gray) so it still reads as "one step down from active", not as dim
" as the FocusLost state (focus_statusline, in the IdeaVim-skip block at the top).
highlight StatusLineNC ctermfg=250 guifg=#888888 ctermbg=22 guibg=#1a3524

" closed folds: bold indigo/purple foreground, no background — visible but
" not a solid highlight block, since most folds (marker folds in this file,
" .zshrc, .tmux.conf) don't need to grab the eye the way Claude transcript
" folds do.
highlight Folded cterm=bold ctermfg=55 ctermbg=NONE gui=bold guifg=#5f00af guibg=NONE

set guifont=MesloLGS-NF-Regular:h13
set linespace=3

